WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:06.270
Speaker 1: Last week, I did a segment for
our TikTok account, which, by the way, Tik

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.550
Tok, over 500,000 followers on TikTok.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:09.760
It's crazy what's going on.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:10.760
We're reaching.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.340
Young people were wild.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.780
Things are happening on TikTok.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:21.070
I did a segment where I laid out why I don't
think the impact of Trump's arrest will be

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:23.410
limited only to the presidential race.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:26.640
And the point I made was that there's going
to be a significant trickle down effect.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.320
Now, I'm wondering whether I did this for
Tik Tok or for our Straight Arrow news partnership.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:35.079
But in any case, I do remember talking about
this maybe even on the bonus show now, I don't

00:00:35.079 --> 00:00:36.079
remember.

00:00:36.079 --> 00:00:43.870
My argument is as follows It would be wrong
to assume that Trump's trials and indictments

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.220
will only affect the presidential race.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:50.590
I believe that it will affect down ballot
Republicans, and it has the potential, depending

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:56.640
on how this all goes over the next 6 to 18
months, to generate an insane amount of chaos

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.890
for Republicans trying to get themselves reelected
in November of 2024.

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:07.020
If you are a pro-Trump acolyte and you're
trying to get reelected and Trump really has

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:12.130
legal issues and is damaged in the primary,
maybe loses it or wins, but then loses to

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:17.520
Joe Biden, it could turn off a lot of people
from voting for their local elected official

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.810
House or Senate for reelection.

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:24.909
On the other hand, if you take the anti-Trump
side as a Republican seeking reelection in

00:01:24.909 --> 00:01:29.770
2024 and Trump prevails, that could end up
being very damaging to you.

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:31.780
So there's a lot of risk here.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:33.850
Too many in the Republican Party.

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:37.619
And as we talked about late last week, Republicans
are worried that Trump is going to drag them

00:01:37.619 --> 00:01:38.670
down.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:44.210
We now are really starting to look at trial
calendars and Republican debates, schedules

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.530
and primary schedules.

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:51.790
And it is hard to come away with any conclusion
other than the one that Newsweek has come

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:57.770
across or come to believe, which is that,
as they say, Donald Trump is likely to be

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:02.850
swamped with multiple overlapping criminal
trials.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:08.319
This is the one scenario other than a health
problem that could derail Donald Trump's campaign.

00:02:08.319 --> 00:02:12.230
Newsweek writes Donald Trump is at risk of
being faced with multiple criminal trials

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:17.239
at the same time, all while campaigning to
become president in 2024.

00:02:17.239 --> 00:02:21.950
Tuesday, Trump pleaded not guilty to 37 federal
offenses connected to the Jackie Smith Documents

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:28.680
case and is expected to appear next in Florida
court in June.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:34.160
It is currently unknown when a trial could
be set for the classified documents case,

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:36.430
with the decision to be made by Judge Eileen
Cannon.

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:40.070
Of course, as we talked about, appointed to
the bench by Trump facing calls to recuse

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:43.210
herself, the article continues.

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:45.690
The New York trial will will take place.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:46.870
This is the other trial.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:50.750
The New York trial will take place while the
Republican primary is well underway.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:55.560
And after the so-called Super Tuesday, where
several states vote on the same day elsewhere,

00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:01.810
there have been indications that the criminal
investigation in Georgia is drawing to a close

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:04.290
and Trump could face former indictments.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:09.569
That's going to be sometime between July and
September, probably here.

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:11.239
They're talking about July and August, etc..

00:03:11.239 --> 00:03:17.030
A Fani Willis is office says federal indictments
will not have any impact on the Fulton County

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:22.140
election investigation, saying what she is
doing is going to happen regardless of what

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.849
is happening federally.

00:03:23.849 --> 00:03:30.209
And then it's also important to remember that
Donald Trump is potentially going to be federal

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:35.200
indictment indicted an additional time related
to January 6th.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.200
So when we.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.709
Think about what could derail Trump.

00:03:37.709 --> 00:03:38.709
A health problem.

00:03:38.709 --> 00:03:39.860
But that could happen to anybody.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.220
Anybody could be derailed by a health problem.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:49.970
The political scenario that could derail Trump
is that he is so flooded with criminal trials

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:52.980
that he quite literally just can't keep campaigning.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:55.540
It pulls him off the campaign trail.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.310
Trump has pledged to stay in regardless.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:58.310
That is his pledge.

00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:00.860
But Trump says things all the time that end
up not being true.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:03.079
This is really a cautionary tale.

00:04:03.079 --> 00:04:07.590
It's best to commit only one crime per year
so that you can keep your schedule clear.

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:09.000
I'm sort of kidding.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.610
Of course, Trump is innocent until proven
guilty.

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:18.359
I still doubt at the end of the day that the
path away from Trump in this primary is that

00:04:18.359 --> 00:04:23.890
he drops out or that the path out of Trump
in this election is that he drops out.

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:27.910
I see it as far more likely that Trump stays
in.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:32.039
Wins the primary but loses to Joe Biden in
2024.

00:04:32.039 --> 00:04:34.330
I believe that is the most likely scenario.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:40.910
The second most likely scenario is Trump stays
in the primary but loses the primary.

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:42.919
Less likely, but still possible.

00:04:42.919 --> 00:04:49.150
And I believe the least likely scenario is
that Donald Trump bails on the primary and

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:52.699
even less likely I think it's Trump dies and
is no longer a candidate.

00:04:52.699 --> 00:04:53.900
I would put that as fourth.

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:58.130
That's my order for this at the end of the
day.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:01.870
It really is up to Republicans to decide what
it is that they want.

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:05.560
And right now, although the polling is moving
a little bit and I know we're going to look

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:08.180
at polling later this week.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:12.580
The polling is moving a little bit, but Trump
is still very much in control.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:18.990
Chris Christie's argument is when you talk
to the Trump supporters today.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:24.970
About half of them or more say I do support
Trump as of today, but I'm open to supporting

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.340
somebody else.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:30.520
Chris Christie's argument is, if you take
the people who are definitely not supporting

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:35.800
Trump in the primary and then you add to that
the number of people supporting Trump but

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:39.430
willing to vote for someone else, that's enough
to win.

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:41.020
And Chris Christie is correct mathematically.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:47.620
The question is, what would it take for that
group that says I support Trump, but I'm willing

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:49.100
to look elsewhere?

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:52.440
What would it take to get them to actually
look elsewhere?

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:56.800
And even two more indictments, I don't believe
is going to change their mind.

